  "body": "The reviewed advertising implementation could use incomplete financial inputs, lose responsibility for unresolved risk, and advance an action without consistently bound human approval and outcome evidence. This rework applies the 22 frozen findings across canonical calculation, human workflow, database authority, transmission, outcomes and disclosure.\n\nFinal-source local and required remote verification in progress; no completion claim.\n\n## Control references\n\n- Product / Slice: V1 / SLICE-V1-003 Advertising & Traffic Efficiency.\n- Immutable Contract: `docs/03-work-items/SLICE-V1-003-advertising-traffic-efficiency.md`; SHA-256 `1606a844934c49a9e67dc0a1a15d49f4003913efc678bae94403c3c29ecb811c`.\n- Accepted Slice003 amendments: NONE. Protected predecessor Contracts, Amendments and Owner evidence remain unchanged.\n- Frozen Finding Set: `docs/07-phase-evidence/SLICE-V1-003/SLICE-V1-003-FROZEN-FINDING-SET-001.md`; SHA-256 `15b3c076fc7f1d283a2c7359d9647d91d3ecfccd9b229be1f734f4e7d4ceefc1`; JSON SHA-256 `f4af74f5086772dc70c3ec3cc7aa8808e9441e96109d301b145e70c18f6131a0`.\n- Exact accepted Owner Decisions / requirements / ADRs are linked per criterion in the [R1 acceptance matrix](docs/07-phase-evidence/SLICE-V1-003/rework-r1/S3-AC-REWORK-STATUS.json). AC001\u2013199 require individual engineering evidence; AC200's independent no-BLOCKER/MAJOR assessment remains pending.\n- Authorization / related request: `OWNER_CODEX_SLICE_V1_003_ROOT_CAUSE_REWORK_R1`, [separate Owner evidence](docs/08-handoffs/OWNER-SLICE-V1-003-CODEX-REWORK-AUTHORIZATION-EVIDENCE.md).\n\n## Observable outcome and scope\n\n- Quantity-weighted canonical economics, explicit purpose freshness and deterministic finite policy targets preserve uncertainty and cause-bound limitations.\n- One cause-owned Task survives concurrent calculation, reassignment, staffed response, accepted risk and invalidation. Exact Maker, Operations and Owner decisions bind the selected candidate and trusted three-stage baseline.\n- Controlled bid creation, immutable leases, aggregate exposure, readback and compensation retain exact scope and evidence. Manual instructions remain governed and do not become Provider command families.\n- Current and historical disclosures respect the complete affected set and actual financial grants. The two platform fixtures exercise real services and browser behavior.\n\nAll changes address the frozen Slice scope. Accepted normative bytes and protected V0001\u2013V0035 remain unchanged. Adjacent inventory writes, Provider choices and production enablement remain outside this authority.\n\n## Change summary\n\n- Backend / database: canonical economics and priority, responsibility and human decisions, sealed SQL authority, six exposure axes, three-stage outcomes and append-only revisions; candidate migrations V0036\u2013V0056 corrected and V0057\u2013V0065 additive.\n- Frontend: scoped operational evidence, explicit unknown impact, governed Manual flows, keyboard and scoped pagination proof.\n- CI / assurance: exact source and artifact identities, actual complete capacity workloads, full protected/fresh migration verification, negative coverage enforcement and all required Draft-safe jobs. Backend full-job budgets are 60 minutes; business SLOs, test workloads and coverage thresholds are unchanged.\n- Documentation: [as-built design](docs/02-architecture/designs/SLICE-V1-003-design.md), coherent runbooks, six traceability shards, [22 finding rows](docs/07-phase-evidence/SLICE-V1-003/rework-r1/FINDING-CLOSURE-MATRIX.json), all 200 accepted criteria and all 24 deferred release obligations.\n\n## Production Assurance evidence\n\n[The R1 evidence index](docs/07-phase-evidence/SLICE-V1-003/rework-r1/README.md) separates immutable historical failures, exact clean measurements, named assertions, source inspection and pending work. A passing aggregate run never automatically closes a finding.\n\n| Assurance boundary | Evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Governance / protected source | Takeover and exact committed-identity receipts; complete governance and independent-clone checks |\n| Unit / property / database / architecture | Complete clean Maven runs, original XML/logs, source and resource manifests; individually named fault and replay assertions |\n| Migration / artifact | All 65 migrations with protected V0001\u2013V0035 byte comparisons; packaged-artifact and managed-runtime evidence |\n| Security / disclosure | Scoped HTTP and browser negatives; secret/JWT evidence scans; required dependency and CodeQL jobs |\n| Browser / frontend | Actual isolated Chromium journeys and fresh lockfile installation with full frontend checks |\n| Provider / readback | Synthetic ports and local fixture servers only; no real Provider verification is claimed |\n| Performance / recovery | Original workload, host/Docker resources, actual capacity and missed-trigger recovery measurements |\n\nLatest-Head check, tested-merge parents/tree, workflow run/attempt/job and artifact identities are collected from GitHub and bound in the final transport receipt; incomplete or skipped checks remain explicitly pending.\n\n## Data, security, AI and controlled write\n\nFixture evidence is synthetic. Real credentials, Buyer PII, Provider endpoints and shared/production environments are excluded from execution. Raw/Ledger/Audit history, idempotency and late/unknown states remain preserved. AI cannot supply Fact, Policy, Approval, Command or credential authority.\n\n`production_write_enabled=false`. All 24 exact [release obligations](docs/07-phase-evidence/SLICE-V1-003/rework-r1/S3-REL-DEFERRED-REGISTER.json) remain production-blocking. Release, Gate EV/E, Pilot, deployment and production verification are not authorized.\n\n## Operational impact\n\nForward migration is limited to the accepted candidate and additive Slice migrations; protected historical migrations are byte-identical. Outcome revisions and authority invalidations are append-only. Runbooks retain explicit replay/reconciliation, quarantine, kill-switch and compensation boundaries. This Draft PR makes no deployment, backfill against a shared database or production rollback request.\n\n## Execution and closure protocol\n\n- Base: `08ad7da7d9e75b4ddd1c387a22ac0affba9e1430`.\n- Reviewed starting Head / tree: `a0711f1ae430e70ab7ec06917004e9dbfd1fb4eb` / `fb4d242d62febd87191da9dce353bdef99f5a77d`.\n- Current source Head / tree: `247ea5ced6cd0ac110314db9fa606d8995c85cac` / `e43d50161faf5b861ee768fa49b66c8b7a407429`.\n- Publisher: Codex under the exact R1 Owner authorization, ordinary append-only push on `feat/SLICE-V1-003-advertising-traffic-efficiency` only. The final transport receipt verifies remote identity and ancestry.\n- All changes address the original Frozen Finding Set; no replacement or amended finding set is introduced. Individual completion and independent closure remain governed by the evidence matrix.\n- Controller Slice Closure / Owner Formal Closure / next-Slice Closure Snapshot: not issued; independent review remains pending.\n\n## AI/agent disclosure\n\nCodex performed the continuous rework with bounded source, normative/control and UI/CI subagents. Exact commands, actual results, prior failures and remaining limitations are retained in the per-run receipts and per-finding matrix. Real release evidence is explicitly deferred only under the accepted Contract; an in-scope engineering gap cannot be deferred as Provider work.\n\n## Owner Git workflow handoff\n\nThe PR remains Draft / Open / Unmerged with no auto-merge. No Ready, self-approval, merge, force-push or direct-main push is authorized. Codex completes the measured engineering/CI record; the next review is independent Controller Final Closure Verification on the exact final Head. Merge would not enable production behavior. No post-merge cleanup or synchronization is performed by this task.\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\nIndependent Controller review must assess the exact diff, all 22 original findings, individual accepted criteria, actual evidence identities and unchanged authority boundaries. This PR supplies engineering evidence and does not pre-fill a reviewer approval or no-BLOCKER/MAJOR verdict.\n",
